menu "ESP Time-Series Recorder"

    config ESP_TIMESERIES_RECORDER_BUFFER_KIB
        int "Internal DRAM buffer size (KiB)"
        range 16 256
        default 128
        help
            Statically reserve this many KiB of contiguous internal DRAM for
            interleaved signed 16-bit samples. The buffer is volatile and is
            not placed in flash or external PSRAM. This complete amount is a
            compile-time RAM cost even while the recorder is EMPTY.

            Capacity is floor(buffer_bytes / (2 * runtime_channel_count)).
            Increasing the sample rate shortens capture duration but does not
            alter the number of records that fit.

    config ESP_TIMESERIES_RECORDER_MAX_CHANNELS
        int "Maximum number of channels"
        range 1 32
        default 16
        help
            Maximum number of signed 16-bit variables in one sample record.
            The actual channel count is selected when the recorder is
            initialized and determines the capture duration. This limit also
            sizes the small per-channel invalid and saturation counter arrays;
            it does not multiply the main sample-buffer reservation.

endmenu
